course: dictionary
lesson: 7774
title: Putting: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have many meanings, so the sentence around it tells you which one to use. «Putting phones away during game night helps everyone pay attention to each other.» The clue is away: the phones are being moved somewhere out of the way. So putting means placing something somewhere.
explain: Putting also appears in phrases, and the whole phrase has its own meaning. Putting on a coat means dressing. Putting off a job means delaying it. Putting up with something means accepting it, even if you do not like it. Read the words after putting to find the phrase.
explain: In golf, putting means hitting the ball gently along the grass towards the hole. It is said to rhyme with «cutting». When you meet putting, ask: what does this sentence mean? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Putting means placing something somewhere, such as putting a book on the shelf.
fact: Phrases with putting: putting on a coat means dressing, putting off a job means delaying it, and putting up with something means accepting it.
fact: In golf, putting means hitting the ball gently along the grass towards the hole. It rhymes with «cutting».
fact: «Putting things right» means making a problem correct again.
fact: Putting is the -ing form of put (put, puts, put, putting), and it can also be a noun in golf.
exercise: «Putting phones away during game night helps everyone pay attention.» What does putting mean in this sentence? | Delaying something until later | Hitting a ball into a hole | Dressing yourself warmly | *Placing something somewhere out of the way
exercise: Ella says «putting on a coat» means taking the coat off. What does putting on mean? | Taking the coat off | Hitting the ball gently | *Dressing, wearing the coat | Waiting until later
exercise: Dad says, «I am putting the ball into the hole with a gentle tap on the grass.» What sport is he playing? | Football | Swimming | *Golf | Tennis
test: Jayden says, «I am putting off my homework until tomorrow.» What does putting off mean? | Hitting it gently along the grass | Doing it straight away | Placing it on a shelf | *Delaying it, leaving it for later
test: Mum says, «I am putting up with the noise.» What does putting up with mean? | *Accepting something you do not like | Making more noise | Ending a game early | Putting something on a shelf
exam: Mia says putting only means hitting a golf ball. Is she right? | Yes, it always means golf | *No, it also means placing something somewhere, like putting toys away | Yes, but only in maths lessons | No, it means dressing only
